    "narrative": "The offensive engine for the Austin Waves today is undoubtedly **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 81.88 efficiency score leads the squad. Facing a favorable 4.32 xERA matchup, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from both a prime leadoff spot and a rare \"Slow SP Delivery\" indicator, which\u2014given our extreme emphasis on stolen base scarcity\u2014makes him our top asset for today's slate. Right behind him, **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Drake Baldwin** (67.38) provide elite value; **Sam Antonacci** leverages a significant SP skill edge (19%) out of the leadoff hole, while **Drake Baldwin** enjoys a potent combination of a 4.62 xERA opposing starter and an 8% boost from batting second. **Kyle Tucker** (67.28) remains a high-floor anchor despite the platoon matchup, with his score buoyed by favorable wind conditions providing a slight power-ceiling lift.\n\nStrategic decisions today centered on the middle infield and utility slots. **Nasim Nunez** (52.28) squeezed into the MI slot despite a negative order penalty because his speed profile remains vital, even against an elite hold pitcher. The most difficult bench decision involved weighing the raw upside of our reserves against the volatility of the bottom-third order spots; **Heliot Ramos** (45.65) narrowly held his position over potential alternates, as the optimizer favored his plate appearance volume over the bench options, which currently remain depleted by the IL stints of **Jordan Westburg** and **Josh Jung**. We are keeping a close watch on the **Liam Hicks** (50.09) matchup against Perkins; while his platoon advantage is strong, he remains our most marginal start, and he will be the first candidate pulled should game-cap management become necessary later in the week.",
